<section id="what-is-local-seo" class="reveal">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-head center">
      <span class="eyebrow">The Work Behind The Ranking</span>
      <h2>What <span class="highlight">local SEO</span> really is</h2>
      <p>No jargon. This is the work we actually do, and why it moves the map.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="explainer">
      <p>
        Local SEO is the work of making one business the obvious answer in one place.
        Someone nearby searches for what you sell. Google picks three businesses for
        the local pack — the map block that sits above the normal search results — and
        those three get the calls. Everyone else gets scrolled past.
      </p>
      <p>
        Google chooses those three on relevance, distance and prominence. You cannot
        move your shop, so a local SEO strategy works the other two. We make the
        business relevant for the searches that actually bring money, and prominent
        enough that the search engine trusts it over the one next door.
      </p>
      <p>That comes down to six concrete jobs, done in order:</p>

      <ul class="explainer-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Google Business Profile</strong> — categories, services, service
          area, photos and posts, set up the way the local pack actually reads them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reviews</strong> — a steady, honest flow, answered properly. This is
          the strongest prominence signal you control.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local landing pages</strong> — one real page per service and per
          area, so a local search has something specific to match.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Citations</strong> — name, address and phone identical everywhere, so
          the search engine is confident this is one business, not three.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical health</strong> — a fast, crawlable site, because a page
          that loads slowly loses the click it just won.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Grid rank tracking</strong> — measured across your whole area instead
          of one centre point, so you see where you really rank.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        None of it is a trick. It is the same six jobs, done properly, every week,
        until the map moves.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<section id="faq" class="reveal">
